      "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.991d06cc097c9eb8e0c300c7b0ac7fbfc38ea1b8.001.1",
      "event": "Flood Advisory",
      "severity": "Minor",
      "urgency": "Expected",
      "certainty": "Likely",
      "headline": "Flood Advisory issued October 28 at 7:23PM HST until October 28 at 9:30PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...Windward side of Honolulu County...\n\n* WHEN...Until 930 PM HST.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding on roads, poor drainage areas, and in\nstreams. Water over roadways.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 718 PM HST, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nheavy rain over areas of windward Oahu. Rain was falling at a\nrate of 0.5 to 1.5 inches per hour in the Kaneohe Bay and Kailua\nareas. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly in\nthe advisory area.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nKaneohe, Kailua, Ahuimanu, Kahaluu, Waiahole, and Waikane.",
      "instruction": "Stay away from streams, drainage ditches and low lying areas prone to\nflooding.\n\nA Flood Watch is also in effect for until 6 AM Thursday HST.",
      "areaDesc": "Oahu in Honolulu, HI",
      "zones": [],
      "effective": "2026-10-28T19:23:00-10:00",
      "expires": "2026-10-28T21:30:00-10:00",
