      "sourceUrl": "https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn%3Aoid%3A2.49.0.1.840.0.991d06cc097c9eb8e0c300c7b0ac7fbfc38ea1b8.001.1"
    },
    {
      "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2f1fdb7fff4e79449e2098e1080ce4b2e84d6f0b.002.1",
      "event": "Flood Watch",
      "severity": "Severe",
      "urgency": "Future",
      "certainty": "Possible",
      "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 28 at 3:29PM HST until October 29 at 5:00AM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "A trough moving over the state is expected to continue to bring\nabundant tropical moisture to the area through tonight. Heavy rain\nand isolated thunderstorms are expected to produce flash flooding\nthat may impact areas across Oahu through the Big Island.\n\n* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Oahu, Molokai, Lanai, Maui, Kahoolawe and The Big Island.\n\n* WHEN...Through late tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Significant flooding may occur due to the overflow of\nstreams and drainages. Roads in several areas may be closed, along\nwith property damage in urban or low lying spots due to runoff.\nLandslides may also occur in areas with steep terrain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Heavy showers and isolated thunderstorms with intense rain rates\nmay develop at any time through tonight as a trough continues\nmoving over the state. While the greatest flood threat will be\nfocused over Oahu and Maui County, all islands are at risk.",
      "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
