  "outlookText": "000\nACPN50 PHFO 290515\nTWOCP \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS Central Pacific Hurricane Center Honolulu HI\nIssued by NWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n800 PM HST Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nFor the central North Pacific...between 140W and 180W:\n\nActive Systems:\nThe National Hurricane Center is issuing advisories on Tropical\nDepression Vance, located about a couple hundred miles\nwest-northwest of Cabo Corrientes, Mexico.\n\nWell Southeast of the Hawaiian Islands:\nA broad area of low pressure could develop well to the southeast of\nthe Hawaiian Islands by this weekend or early next week. Thereafter,\nenvironmental conditions appear generally favorable for some slow\ndevelopment of this system as it moves westward to\nwest-northwestward into the Central Pacific basin.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...30 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Blake\nNNNN",
